&lt;&lt;~ set lares=`aim` from=`lar://operator:human@hearth/device.scope.requests` to=`lar://device-wright:agent@hearth/device.scope.reports` ooda-ha=`2/declare-aftermath` drift-ward=`the full node and browser suites report failures outside the focused placement checks`>>

Device-Wright: Lares (Tasked Spirit): Implemented the vessel-scoped daemon canon pointer and slots. The focused tests pass, but the full node and browser suites do not pass.

The control document now names canon documents under `bags/control/daemon-canon/<encoded-face-relation>` and daemon slots under `bags/control/daemon-slot/<kind>/<encoded-persona-group>`. The slot resolver returns vessel-only reach for the daemon and retains the existing path for user wikis. Surface resolution accepts a recipe carrying `canonBag`. The promote candidate reader still uses `wikiBagUri`: it receives a slug and catalog, with no recipe in hand.

Changed files:

* Node and browser: `face-daemon-canon.ts`, `open-*-vessel.ts`, and their canon tests.
* Keyhive: `slot-doc-resolver.ts`, `operator-daemon-behavior.ts`, and the resolver and working-attachment tests.
* Mesh: `surface-recipe.ts`, `wiki-recipe.ts`, and `surface-mount.test.ts`.
* Node: `faced-boot-requires-proof.test.ts`, whose fixed source window needed expansion after the browser call grew.

Validation:

* Builds and stamps completed for mesh, keyhive, TW5, node, and browser; all five typechecks passed.
* Focused tests passed: mesh surface ''30/30'', keyhive resolver ''9/9'', keyhive working attachment ''7/7'', node canon ''7/7'', browser canon ''4/4'', and node face-proof source check ''10/10''.
* Full keyhive suite: ''561 passed'' across 97 files.
* Full node suite: ''3,261 passed, 204 failed, 51 skipped, 3 expected failures''. Of the failures, 178 reported `secret-home-unavailable`, 13 hit the read-only filesystem, 2 timed out, and 11 reported other causes. One of those 11 was the source-window test corrected and passed afterward; the remaining full-suite failures have not been resolved.
* Full browser suite: ''517 passed, 19 failed, 10 skipped, 1 expected failure''. All 19 failures reported `secret-home-unavailable`.
* `evergreen-boundary.mjs`, `placement-residency-witness.sh`, and `git diff --check` passed.

The requested red-first sequence did not happen: implementation edits preceded the new tests.

->↺ The focused placement checks landed; the full-suite failures remain visible for their respective seats.

